Summary of Logical Relationships

• G1 (Complete Resource Collection and Delivery Mission) → G1.1 (Resource Collection Phase), G1.2 (Resource Delivery Phase), G1.3 (Multi-Robot Coordination) [AND/OR]  
  **Justification:** The overall mission is broken into two mandatory phases (collection and delivery, AND) plus an optional multi-robot coordination phase (OR) that is activated when multiple storages/items are involved.

• G1.1 (Resource Collection Phase) → AT1, AT2, AT3, AT5 [AND with Fallback]  
  **Justification:** The collection phase requires sequential execution of navigation, resource requesting, and waiting—with a fallback branch (AT5) to manage low battery situations.

• G1.2 (Resource Delivery Phase) → AT6, AT7, AT8, AT9 [AND with Fallback]  
  **Justification:** Delivery is executed in sequence (navigate, deliver, monitor battery) with a fallback branch (AT9) to handle low battery conditions during delivery.

• G1.3 (Multi-Robot Coordination) → AT10 [AND]  
  **Justification:** When multiple items or storages are involved, multiple robots must be assigned concurrently to reduce mission time, achieved via the task AT10.

